Feature addition: WASM Rapier.js collision detection with SpatialHash fallback.

This commit modifies 6 files (+1658 lines), spanning 3 TypeScript source, 2 tests, 1 documentation.
This feature extends the Geometry Wars 3D codebase with new functionality. The implementation follows the project's established patterns and maintains compatibility with both single-player and multiplayer code paths where applicable.

Additional context from the commit body:
RapierWorld (389 lines) + CollisionBridge (205 lines) + CollisionGroups.
Async WASM init with automatic SpatialHash fallback. Benchmarks show
SpatialHash faster at current entity counts (1K: 0.86ms vs 1.56ms),
but Rapier enables collision group filtering and future non-sphere shapes.
54 tests passing including 1K/5K/10K entity benchmarks.

